fix(servers): right-clicking a server row stops risking a Keychain prompt in front of the menu

`openServerRowMenu` read `hasServerSecret` to decide whether to draw "Forget saved password". That is a Keychain read on
the right-click path, and every read of one can raise a system prompt: the exact cost the comment beside it said moving
the question off Rust's popup path avoided. `servers/DETAILS.md` justified the difference from SMB's never-pre-check
rule by claiming SFTP's `has_*` is cheaper, which is false: `commands/sftp.rs` calls `network::keychain::has_credentials`,
which is literally `get_credentials(server, share).is_ok()` — the same call `has_smb_credentials` makes.

So the item is offered on every server row, and the command answers instead. `forget_server_secret` already reports
whether an entry was there; that `false` now gets a sentence
(`fileExplorer.navigation.forgetSecretNoneToast`, "There was no saved password for {name}.") rather than silence after a
confirm dialog. A `true` still says nothing: the entry is gone, which is what the person asked for.

- `ServerRowMenu` loses `has_saved_secret` on both sides of the wire, so nothing can reintroduce the read to fill it.
- `menu_structure.rs` appends the item unconditionally, `busy` gating unchanged.
- `servers/DETAILS.md`'s rationale is corrected: the two reads cost the same, and the question is WHEN paying is worth
  it. A sheet opening is a moment someone is already waiting through; a right-click is not.
- The stale `server-row-actions.ts` comment claiming `pin` / `unpin` / `edit` have no producer is corrected too. Only
  `open` is producerless.

Cells: the menu path never touching the Keychain, the toast on an empty store, and silence on a real one. Ten
translations for the new key, its "saved password" term taken from each locale's own `menu.network.forgetSavedPassword`
so the toast matches the item the user just picked.
